  ('bavaria-germany', '01F', 'Bavaria', 'Germany', 'Beer halls and fairy-tale castles, alpine lakes and medieval', 'live', 'verified', 'kyoto', 'Bavaria & the Alpine South', '{"culture","entertainment","wellness","family","culinary","ski"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Germany''s largest + most-visited state; Munich = capital + node FLAGSHIP + base","Own hub content = the Bavarian Lakes: Chiemsee (Schloss Herrenchiemsee), Starnberger See, Tegernsee","Castles + Alps along the south (Neuschwanstein, Zugspitze 2,962m, Berchtesgaden/Konigssee)","Franconia''s old towns north (Nuremberg, Bamberg, Regensburg, Rothenburg/Romantic Road)","Bavaria-Austria seam: Berchtesgaden in this node; Salzburg in the Austria node (cross-link, no double-cover)","Germany''s most-visited state: ~100.26M overnight stays 2023 (~20.6% national); Upper Bavaria ~40M, a third in Munich","Oktoberfest ~6.5M visitors / ~6.5M litres 2025 (record ~7.2M in 2023); Theresienwiese; 19 Sep-4 Oct 2026","Neuschwanstein ~1.3M visitors/yr (up to 6,000/day summer), begun 1869 by Ludwig II; UNESCO inscription 12 Jul 2025 (Ludwig II palaces serial property, Germany''s 55th site)","German Alpine Road (Deutsche Alpenstrasse) ~484 km Lindau-to-Konigssee; 20+ lakes, 60+ villages, the region''s scenic through-line","Chiemsee ~80 km2 (max 73.4 m, Germany''s 3rd-largest); Herreninsel 238 ha (Herrenchiemsee, begun 1878) + Fraueninsel 15.5 ha; Prien ~57 min from Munich","Reinheitsgebot (Beer Purity Law) adopted 23 Apr 1516 — among the world''s oldest food laws still in force; Bavaria/Franconia = Europe''s densest brewery country","Nuremberg Christkindlesmarkt ~2M visitors/yr, 180+ stalls, first recorded 1530; Advent tentpole of Bavaria''s December","Ski picture: Zugspitze glacier (~2,600-2,720 m, Germany''s highest pistes) + Allgau/Oberstdorf (Nebelhorn 2,224 m, Germany''s longest run ~7.5 km; Fellhorn/Kanzelwand ~36 km cross-border) — each town its own dossier","