  ('cassis-france', '01F', 'Cassis & the Calanques', 'France', 'A pastel fishing port beneath white-cliff coves and a', 'live', 'verified', 'venice', 'Provence & the Riviera', '{"romance","adventure","culinary","wine","family","culture"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'emerging', '{"key_facts":["Cassis fishing-port village under Cap Canaille (~394 m, among Europe''s highest sea cliffs)","Cassidain calanques: Port-Miou, Port-Pin, En-Vau (En-Vau the showpiece; boat or hike)","Boat cruises from the port year-round weather-permitting (3-cove ~45 min; 5- and 9-cove circuits)","Route des Cretes ~15 km clifftop road Cassis->La Ciotat over the Soubeyran cliffs","Cassis AOC: ~210 ha urban vineyard, ~1 M bottles/yr, whites 67%, appellation since 1936","SUMMER FIRE ACCESS: massif land access regulated 1 Jun-30 Sep; red days = 24 h walking ban; daily Prefecture map (~6pm next-day)"],"safety":{"emergency":"112 / 15 SAMU / 17 police / 18 pompiers / 114 SMS","hospital":"CH Aubagne (Edmond Garcin) nearest; AP-HM La Timone Marseille trauma ~30-40 min","advisory_level":"L2","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","activity_note":"Calanques land access fire-regulated day-by-day 1 Jun-30 Sep (red = 24h walking ban; check daily Prefecture map); exposed limestone/no shade/steep drops; Mistral for boating/kayak; sheer unfenced drops at Cap Canaille/Route des Cretes"},"timing":{"peak":"Jul-Aug (summer, hottest/busiest) — Calanques land access fire-restricted; boats carry the coves","shoulder":"May-Jun, Sep (sweet spot — boats running, massif more reliably open; Sep harvest)","green":"Nov-Mar (village + wine + Route des Cretes open; boats reduced/weather-dependent)","booking_lead":"summer + Cap Canaille villas 2-4 mo (Aug + weekends tightest); shoulder ~2-3 wk","off_season_specials":"Nov-Mar village-and-wine breaks, Route des Cretes drives, long-weekend rates","event_peaks":"summer beach + boat season (~Apr-Oct), Cassis wine harvest (Sep), village